# Macroeconomics for development in Latin America and the Caribbean: New thoughts on countercyclicality

**Authors:** D. Titelman, Esteban Pérez-Caldentey

## Abstract
Macroeconomics for development in Latin America and the Caribbean is traditionally structured around two issues: an active production development and diversification strategy and a countercyclical policy stance (Ocampo, 2011; Ffrench-Davis, 2010).

